    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾱο-σσόος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rousing</i> or <i>stirring the nations</i>, epith.
			of the war-deities Ares, Eris, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20.48
			</span></i>; of Athena, <i><span class="en">
				13.128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.210
			</span></i>; of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.79
			</span></i>: also of men, as Amphiaraus, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.244
			</span></i>; of Electryon, Amphitryon, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				3
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				37
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαοσσόοι ἀγῶνες</span>
			assemblies <i>to which the people flock</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.24
			</span></i>.</div>
